<div class="single-topic-subs-grid">
  <div class="subs-item">
    <h3>Define the Why, the Win, and the Way</h3>
    <p>Clarify the problem, the measurable outcomes, and the first three behaviors that must change. Keep it on one page you can revisit at stand-ups, reviews, and retros.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="subs-item">
    <h3>Equip Credible Champions</h3>
    <p>Map stakeholders, risks, and resistance. Recruit trusted champions—project leads and client-facing roles—and give them talk tracks, FAQs, and quick demos to lower friction and build trust.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="subs-item">
    <h3>Make It Stick in the Work</h3>
    <p>Embed the change into existing rhythms: kickoff checklists, status updates, QA gates, and handoffs. Run short pilots, show visible progress, and use tight feedback loops to adjust fast.</p>
  </div>
</div>
